quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  4,27,"And Allah intends to turn to you in mercy, but those who follow their lusts want you to deviate (entirely from the path of guidance) into a severe deviation."
  4,28,"Allah intends to lighten your burden, for humans are created weak."
  4,29,"O believers! Do not wrongfully consume your wealth among yourselves, but it should be a trade by mutual consent. And do not kill yourselves. Indeed, Allah is All-Merciful to you."
  4,30,"And whoever does that aggressively or unjustly, We shall soon cause him to burn in the Fire. And that is easy for Allah."
  4,31,"If you avoid the major sins you have been forbidden, We shall wipe out your minor sins and admit you (into Paradise) through an honourable entrance."
  4,32,"Do not covet the blessings Allah has graced upon some of you above others. To men belongs a share of what they earn, and to women a share of what they earn. Ask Allah from His grace; surely Allah is All-Knowing of everything."
  4,33,"For everyone, We have appointed heirs to what parents and near relatives leave behind, including those to whom you have pledged your hands (in marriage), so give them their share (of inheritance). Indeed, Allah is a Witness over all things."
